    <fr:title text="Add has-meta Datalog Relation">Add has-meta Datalog Relation</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>TODO</fr:taxon>
    <fr:meta name="status">cancelled</fr:meta>
    <fr:meta name="completed">2026-05-29</fr:meta>
    <fr:meta name="cancelled">true</fr:meta>
    <fr:meta name="priority">medium</fr:meta>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>Add a built-in <html:code><![CDATA[\rel/has-meta]]></html:code> Datalog relation to the forester fork so that trees can be queried by <html:code><![CDATA[\meta{...}{...}]]></html:code> values, not just by tags.</html:p>
    <html:p>Motivation: task status is currently tracked redundantly via both <html:code><![CDATA[\tag{status-*}]]></html:code> (for Datalog) and <html:code><![CDATA[\meta{status}{...}]]></html:code> (for the XSL display badge). With <html:code><![CDATA[\rel/has-meta]]></html:code>, the tags become unnecessary and status lives in one place.</html:p>
    <html:p>Example query after this change:</html:p>
    <html:pre><![CDATA[\query\datalog{
  ?X -:
    {\rel/has-taxon ?X '{TODO}}
    {\rel/has-meta ?X '{status} '{pending}}
}]]></html:pre>
    <html:p>Implementation sketch — three places to touch in <html:code>~/ocaml-forester</html:code>:</html:p>
    <html:ul><html:li><html:strong><html:code>lib/core/Builtin_relation.ml</html:code></html:strong>: add <html:code>let has_meta = make_builtin "has-meta"</html:code> alongside <html:code>has_tag</html:code>, <html:code>has_taxon</html:code>, etc.</html:li>
  <html:li><html:strong>Population logic</html:strong> (wherever <html:code>has-tag</html:code> facts are asserted from <html:code>fr:tag</html:code> elements): iterate over each <html:code>fr:meta name="K" value="V"</html:code> and assert <html:code>has_meta(tree_id, K, V)</html:code>.</html:li>
  <html:li><html:strong>Datalog arity</html:strong>: <html:code>has-tag</html:code> is binary; <html:code>has-meta</html:code> needs to be ternary (<html:code>?X</html:code>, key, value) — verify <html:code>lib/core/Datalog_engine.ml</html:code> supports 3-arity or adapt.</html:li></html:ul>
    <html:p>Once landed, migrate dashboard/todos/finished queries off <html:code><![CDATA[\rel/has-tag ?X '{status-*}]]></html:code> and drop <html:code><![CDATA[\tag{status-*}]]></html:code> from TODO trees in favor of <html:code><![CDATA[\meta{status}{...}]]></html:code> alone.</html:p>
    <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
      <fr:frontmatter>
        <fr:authors>
          <fr:author>
            <fr:link href="/stevenschaefer/" title="Steven Schaefer" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/stevenschaefer/" display-uri="stevenschaefer" type="local">Steven Schaefer</fr:link>
          </fr:author>
        </fr:authors>
        <fr:date>
