      <fr:mainmatter>
        <html:p>Several pieces of software read or write <html:code><![CDATA[\tag{status-*}]]></html:code> and will need updating once the migration is complete:</html:p>
        <html:ul><html:li><html:strong><html:code>forester-org.el</html:code></html:strong> (<html:code>~/ocaml-forester/forester-org.el</html:code>): the primary Emacs mode for managing todos. Three sites need updating: <html:code>forester-capture-todo</html:code> and <html:code>forester-todo-here</html:code> (which write <html:code><![CDATA[\tag{status-pending}]]></html:code> on creation but no <html:code><![CDATA[\meta{status}]]></html:code>); <html:code>forester-org--current-todo-state</html:code> (reads state by scanning for <html:code>status-</html:code> tag prefix); and <html:code>forester-cycle-todo-state</html:code> (cycles by replacing the tag only, not updating <html:code><![CDATA[\meta{status}]]></html:code>). The <html:code>forester-org--collect-todos</html:code> function similarly infers status from the tag. After the feature lands, these should write/read <html:code><![CDATA[\meta{status}]]></html:code> instead.</html:li>
  <html:li><html:strong>Claude skills</html:strong>: <html:code>start-coding</html:code> greps for <html:code><![CDATA[\tag{status-pending}]]></html:code> and <html:code><![CDATA[\tag{status-in-progress}]]></html:code> to surface active TODOs. These greps will need to switch to matching <html:code><![CDATA[\meta{status}]]></html:code> patterns.</html:li></html:ul>
      </fr:mainmatter>
